 ## Overview
-This method rasterizes Ellipsoid-Warping (EWA) splats on general-purpose graphics hardware by treating point primitives as screen-space squares and casting a viewing ray for each fragment to test inclusion within the splat's volume [S2, unofficial]. It distinguishes itself from polygon-based bounding approximations (e.g., Botsch et al.) by providing a correct upper bound to splat extents that remains stable for large splats near the near plane, while avoiding the numerical instabilities of explicit conic centralization or matrix inversions [S1][S2, unofficial].
+This method rasterizes Ellipsoid-Wise Adaptive (EWA) splats on general-purpose graphics hardware by treating point primitives as screen-space squares and casting a viewing ray for each fragment to test inclusion within the splat's volume [S2, unofficial]. It distinguishes itself from polygon-based bounding approximations (e.g., Botsch et al.) by providing a correct upper bound to splat extents that remains stable for large splats near the near plane, while avoiding the numerical instabilities of explicit conic centralization or matrix inversions [S1][S2, unofficial].
 
